            </div>
            <div class="duo claude-code">
              <div class="duo-title">claude code</div>
              <div class="chip-stack">
                {claudeCodeItems.map((s) => <div class="chip">{s}</div>)}
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="maturity">
            <div class="maturity-head">
              <div class="maturity-title">
                ai engineering practices · reifegrad
              </div>
              <div class="maturity-meta">
                re-audit v3 · stand 31.05.2026 · 38 / 90 · 42 % maturity (von
                33 %)
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="maturity-note">Die niedrigen Felder sind kein Versäumnis, sondern eine Entscheidung: umgesetzt wurde, was den Punkt beweist, nicht was die Tabelle füllt. Ein ehrlicher Stand sagt mehr als ein geschönter.</p>

            <div class="maturity-legend">
              {
                maturityLegend.map((l) => (
                  <span class="legend-item">
                    <span
                      class="legend-box"
                      style={`background:${l.bg}; color:${l.fg};`}
                    >
                      {l.lvl}
                    </span>
                    {l.text}
                  </span>
                ))
              }
            </div>

            {
              pillars.map((p) => (
                <div class="pillar">
                  <div
                    class="pillar-head"
                    style={`border-left-color:${p.accent};`}
                  >
                    <span>
                      {p.letter} · {p.title}
                    </span>
                    <span class="pillar-score" style={`color:${p.accent};`}>
                      {p.score}
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  <div class="pillar-items">
                    {p.items.map((it) => {
                      const tone = maturityLegend[it.level];
                      return (
                        <div class="pillar-item">
                          <span>{it.name}</span>
                          <span
                            class="lvl-pill"
                            style={`background:${tone.bg}; color:${tone.fg};`}
                          >
                            {it.level}
                          </span>
                        </div>
                      );
                    })}
                  </div>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>

          <div class="block">
            <div class="block-title">shared workspace · 15 ADRs</div>
            <div class="tag-row">
              {adrTags.map((t) => <span class="tag mono">{t}</span>)}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="block">
            <div class="block-title">tools &amp; plattformen</div>
            <div class="block-body">
              claude.ai · claude code · github · localhost:5678 · browser
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================ TAB 6: ERKENNTNISSE (PDF.js Viewer) ============================ -->
  <section data-panel="erkenntnisse" role="tabpanel" hidden>
    <div class="tab-sub">
      The Agentic Blueprint, Erkenntnisse aus dem Engineering, im Browser gerendert
      mit PDF.js. Wird beim ersten Tab-Wechsel nachgeladen (~19&nbsp;MB).
    </div>

    <div
      class="pdf-viewer"
      data-pdf-id="erkenntnisse"
      data-pdf-src="/pdf/the-agentic-blueprint.pdf"
    >
      <div class="pdf-toolbar">
        <div class="pdf-toolbar-group">
          <button
            class="pdf-btn"
            data-pdf-action="prev"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Vorherige Seite">←</button
          >
          <span class="pdf-pagecount">
            Seite <span data-pdf-page>—</span> / <span data-pdf-pages>—</span>
          </span>
          <button
            class="pdf-btn"
            data-pdf-action="next"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Nächste Seite">→</button
          >
        </div>
        <div class="pdf-toolbar-group">
          <button
            class="pdf-btn"
            data-pdf-action="zoom-out"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Verkleinern">−</button
          >
          <span class="pdf-zoom" data-pdf-zoom>Fit</span>
          <button
            class="pdf-btn"
            data-pdf-action="zoom-in"
            type="button"
            aria-label="Vergrößern">+</button
          >
          <button
            class="pdf-btn pdf-btn-text"
            data-pdf-action="zoom-fit"
            type="button">↔ Fit</button
          >
        </div>
        <div class="pdf-toolbar-group">
          <a
            class="pdf-btn pdf-btn-text"
            href="/pdf/the-agentic-blueprint.pdf"
            download="The_Agentic_Blueprint.pdf">
            ⬇ Download
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pdf-canvas-wrap" data-pdf-canvas-wrap>
        <div data-pdf-status class="pdf-status">
          PDF wird geladen…
        </div>
        <canvas data-pdf-canvas class="pdf-canvas"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="augur-tieback">
    <p>Das eigentliche Thema ist nicht der Code. Es ist, was die Entwicklung über das Führen einer Organisation durch Agentic AI lehrt: Der Engpass sitzt nicht im Modell, sondern in den hundert Entscheidungen, die das System an Menschen zurückgibt. Wer für das Ergebnis geradesteht, entscheidet diese Phase. Das System kann Arbeit erzeugen. Verantwortung bleibt beim Menschen.</p>
    <p class="augur-tieback-link">Der Commercial-Beweis dazu: <a href="/agentic-ai/sem-agentic">sem-agentic — Google-Ads-SEM-Kampagnensteuerung →</a></p>
  </div>
</SubPageLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    const tabs = document.querySelectorAll("[data-tab]");
    const panels = document.querySelectorAll("[data-panel]");

    function activate(name) {
      tabs.forEach(function (t) {
        const active = t.getAttribute("data-tab") === name;
        t.classList.toggle("tab-active", active);
        t.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(active));
      });
      panels.forEach(function (p) {
        p.hidden = p.getAttribute("data-panel") !== name;
      });
      if (history.replaceState) {
        history.replaceState(null, "", "#" + name);
      }
    }

    tabs.forEach(function (t) {
      t.addEventListener("click", function () {
        activate(t.getAttribute("data-tab"));
      });
    });

    const hash = (window.location.hash || "").slice(1);
    if (
      hash === "working-map" ||
      hash === "reflexionen" ||
      hash === "erkenntnisse"
    ) {
      activate(hash);
    }
  })();
</script>

<!-- PDF.js viewer — Multi-Instance support, lazy-loaded via dynamic import.
     Jeder [data-pdf-id="..."] Container ist eine eigenständige Viewer-Instanz
     mit eigenem State (currentPage, currentScale, doc, renderTask).            -->
<script>
  type Lib = typeof import("pdfjs-dist");

  interface ViewerState {
    id: string;
    pdfUrl: string;
    container: HTMLElement;
    doc: import("pdfjs-dist").PDFDocumentProxy | null;
    currentPage: number;
    currentScale: number | "fit";
    renderTask: import("pdfjs-dist").RenderTask | null;
    initialised: boolean;
    canvas: HTMLCanvasElement;
    wrap: HTMLElement;
    pageEl: Element | null;
    pagesEl: Element | null;
    zoomEl: Element | null;
    statusEl: HTMLElement | null;
  }

  let pdfLib: Lib | null = null;
  const viewers = new Map<string, ViewerState>();

  async function ensurePdfLib(): Promise<Lib> {
    if (pdfLib) return pdfLib;
    const [lib, workerUrl] = await Promise.all([
      import("pdfjs-dist"),
      import("pdfjs-dist/build/pdf.worker.min.mjs?url"),
    ]);
    lib.GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc = workerUrl.default;
    pdfLib = lib;
    return lib;
  }

  function getViewer(container: HTMLElement): ViewerState | null {
    const id = container.dataset.pdfId;
    if (!id) return null;
    const cached = viewers.get(id);
    if (cached) return cached;
    const canvas = container.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>(
      "[data-pdf-canvas]",
    );
    const wrap = container.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-pdf-canvas-wrap]");
    if (!canvas || !wrap) return null;
    const state: ViewerState = {
      id,
      pdfUrl: container.dataset.pdfSrc || "",
      container,
      doc: null,
      currentPage: 1,
      currentScale: "fit",
      renderTask: null,
      initialised: false,
      canvas,
      wrap,
      pageEl: container.querySelector("[data-pdf-page]"),
      pagesEl: container.querySelector("[data-pdf-pages]"),
      zoomEl: container.querySelector("[data-pdf-zoom]"),
      statusEl: container.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-pdf-status]"),
    };
    viewers.set(id, state);
    return state;
  }

  function updateMeta(v: ViewerState) {
    if (v.pageEl) v.pageEl.textContent = String(v.currentPage);
    if (v.pagesEl) v.pagesEl.textContent = v.doc ? String(v.doc.numPages) : "—";
    if (v.zoomEl) {
      v.zoomEl.textContent =
        v.currentScale === "fit"
          ? "Fit"
          : Math.round((v.currentScale as number) * 100) + "%";
    }
  }

  async function renderPage(v: ViewerState, pageNum: number) {
    if (!v.doc) return;
    if (v.renderTask) {
      try {
        v.renderTask.cancel();
      } catch {}
      v.renderTask = null;
    }
    const page = await v.doc.getPage(pageNum);
    const containerWidth = Math.max(280, v.wrap.clientWidth - 16);
    const baseViewport = page.getViewport({ scale: 1 });
    const fitScale = containerWidth / baseViewport.width;
    const finalScale =
      v.currentScale === "fit" ? fitScale : (v.currentScale as number);
    const viewport = page.getViewport({ scale: finalScale });
    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
    v.canvas.width = Math.floor(viewport.width * dpr);
    v.canvas.height = Math.floor(viewport.height * dpr);
    v.canvas.style.width = viewport.width + "px";
    v.canvas.style.height = viewport.height + "px";
    const ctx = v.canvas.getContext("2d");
    if (!ctx) return;
    ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
    v.renderTask = page.render({ canvasContext: ctx, viewport });
    try {
      await v.renderTask.promise;
    } catch {
      // cancelled — fine
    }
    v.renderTask = null;
    updateMeta(v);
  }

  async function initViewer(v: ViewerState) {
    if (v.initialised) return;
    v.initialised = true;
    try {
      const lib = await ensurePdfLib();
      if (v.statusEl) v.statusEl.textContent = "Dokument wird gelesen…";
      const task = lib.getDocument({
        url: v.pdfUrl,
        cMapUrl: "https://unpkg.com/pdfjs-dist@6.0.227/cmaps/",
        cMapPacked: true,
      });
      v.doc = await task.promise;
      if (v.statusEl) v.statusEl.style.display = "none";
      v.currentScale = "fit";
      v.currentPage = 1;
      await renderPage(v, 1);
    } catch (e) {
      console.error(e);
      if (v.statusEl) {
        v.statusEl.textContent =
          "PDF konnte nicht geladen werden: " + (e as Error).message;
      }
      v.initialised = false;
    }
  }

  function bindControls() {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-pdf-action]").forEach(
      function (btn) {
        btn.addEventListener("click", async function () {
          const container = btn.closest<HTMLElement>("[data-pdf-id]");
          if (!container) return;
          const v = getViewer(container);
          if (!v || !v.doc) return;
          const action = btn.dataset.pdfAction;
          if (action === "prev" && v.currentPage > 1) {
            v.currentPage--;
            await renderPage(v, v.currentPage);
          } else if (
            action === "next" &&
            v.doc &&
            v.currentPage < v.doc.numPages
          ) {
            v.currentPage++;
            await renderPage(v, v.currentPage);
          } else if (action === "zoom-in") {
            const base =
              v.currentScale === "fit" ? 1 : (v.currentScale as number);
            v.currentScale = Math.min(3, base + 0.25);
            await renderPage(v, v.currentPage);
          } else if (action === "zoom-out") {
            const base =
              v.currentScale === "fit" ? 1 : (v.currentScale as number);
            v.currentScale = Math.max(0.25, base - 0.25);
            await renderPage(v, v.currentPage);
          } else if (action === "zoom-fit") {
            v.currentScale = "fit";
            await renderPage(v, v.currentPage);
          }
        });
      },
    );
  }

  function maybeInitOnTab() {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-pdf-id]").forEach(
      function (container) {
        const panel = container.closest<HTMLElement>("[data-panel]");
        if (!panel) return;
        const panelName = panel.getAttribute("data-panel");
        if (!panelName) return;
        const tab = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(
          '[data-tab="' + panelName + '"]',
        );
        if (tab) {
          tab.addEventListener("click", function () {
            const v = getViewer(container);
            if (v && !v.initialised) initViewer(v);
          });
        }
        if (window.location.hash === "#" + panelName) {
          const v = getViewer(container);
          if (v) initViewer(v);
        }
      },
    );
  }

  // Re-render alle Viewer in fit mode bei Resize
  let resizeTimer: number | undefined;
  window.addEventListener("resize", function () {
    if (resizeTimer) window.clearTimeout(resizeTimer);
    resizeTimer = window.setTimeout(function () {
      viewers.forEach(function (v) {
        if (v.currentScale === "fit" && v.doc) {
          renderPage(v, v.currentPage);
        }
      });
    }, 200);
  });

  bindControls();
  maybeInitOnTab();
</script>

